A FIFO at .yoyo/goal.md or .yoyo/memory.json no longer hangs startup. It's committed as 31c0cd46, titled "Part of #1047", because .yoyo.toml is still open.

Re-running the reproduction (temp git repo, timeout 25 yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG" </dev/null):
• FIFO at .yoyo/goal.md: exit 0 in 2.0s (the assessment saw a hang and exit 124). It prints ⚠ goal file .yoyo/goal.md not loaded into the prompt — ./.yoyo/goal.md is not a regular file (FIFO): ….
• FIFO at .yoyo/memory.json: exit 0 in 1.7s, with warning: project memories not loaded - … (FIFO) ….

What changed:
• `src/commands_goal.rs`: load_goal_in and load_verify_command now share one helper, read_goal_family_file, which reads through non_regular_read::read_regular_to_string. If the file is a FIFO, device or socket, it prints a warning and carries on as if the file were absent. For goal.md the warning comes from the existing goal_file_refused_warning; goal_verify.md gets its own "verify command … not loaded" line. A missing, blank or unreadable file behaves exactly as before, with no warning.
• `src/memory.rs`: load_memories_from goes through the same reader, so a non-regular memory.json gets a warning and an empty store. Missing or unparseable files still give an empty store silently, as before.
• Docs: the FIFO entry in common-issues.md now lists the goal and memory files as covered; only .yoyo.toml is still named as hanging.

Tests (unix only, using a real mkfifo):
• The FIFO tests run each loader on a thread with recv_timeout(5s), so a regression fails by name instead of hanging the suite. They cover goal.md, goal_verify.md and memory.json.
• A regular goal.md and verify file load to exact trimmed values. Regular and symlinked memory.json load identically, compared with assert_eq! on the entries. A missing or blank file gives None or an empty store with no warning.
• I didn't add a separate goal-symlink test: an existing test fixture already loads a symlinked goal.md and still passes.
• Positive controls, run one at a time, each as a single break-run-restore command: switching each loader back to plain std::fs::read_to_string (marked NEUTERED) made the two goal FIFO tests and the memory FIFO test time out and fail by name. After restoring, everything passed and no markers were left.

cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo build and the full cargo test all pass. The commit body notes that .yoyo.toml (src/config.rs) is left on #1047 because of its size-gate headroom, and points to #1050 as the upstream report.
